# Scripts keep their line endings.
#
# A shebang has to be on the very first line. When a script is checked out with
# CRLF endings the bundler stops recognising the shebang, moves it off the first
# line, and the file then fails to parse with "Invalid or unexpected token".
# That is invisible on Linux, where the files are already LF.
#
# A CRLF shell script is not runnable either.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
